('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','900Wh for $2,399. The NCM T7s is the joint cheapest big battery in the eBikeFinder directory: 912Wh, up to 180km claimed range, 29kg, 250W pedal assist, no throttle, $2,399 drive-away. Only 11 road-legal, no throttle bikes among the 330 we compare pack 900Wh or more, and the NCM M7 matches this price. The 180km figure is a best case eco mode claim, and road-legal status is declared by the brand, so confirm both with the seller. Method: declared road-legal, no throttle, 900Wh or more, lowest price, checked 4 Oct 2026. Full specs: https://ebikefinder.au/ebikes/ncm/t7s Big battery or lighter bike, which would you take? #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-05-mon-am-image.jpg'],'2026-10-04T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-05-am-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','900Wh for $2,399. The NCM T7s is the joint cheapest big battery in the eBikeFinder directory: 912Wh, up to 180km claimed range, 29kg, 250W pedal assist, no throttle, $2,399 drive-away. Only 11 road-legal, no throttle bikes in the directory pack 900Wh or more, and the NCM M7 matches this price. Treat 180km as a best case eco figure. FINDER DATA, 330 bikes compared. Big battery or lighter bike, which would you take? Link in bio. #ebike #ebikeaustralia #commuterebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-05-mon-am-image.jpg'],'2026-10-04T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-05-am-ig','roxy',null),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','5 bikes, about $3,500, wildly different. We pulled five from the 330 in the eBikeFinder directory: ADO Air 20 Ultra folder (22kg, $3,499 ride-away), AMPD Bros Chubbie 3 fat tyre (960Wh, $3,490), Aventon Aventure M (100Nm mid-drive, $3,499 sale price at iScoot; Aventon is distributed in Australia by BikesOnline), Cube Supreme Hybrid ONE 500 (Bosch mid-drive, $3,499 at 99 Bikes) and Pedal Eagle ST ($3,399). Same money, 22kg to 44.5kg and 346Wh to 960Wh. Method: brand declared road-legal, no throttle, listed from $3,399 to $3,499, in stock, prices checked 21 to 27 Sep 2026. Claimed ranges are best case. Compare them side by side: https://ebikefinder.au/compare?bikes=ado/air-20-ultra,ampd-bros/chubbie-3,aventon/aventure-m,cube/supreme-hybrid-one-500,pedal/eagle-st Which one would you buy? #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-4.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-5.jpg'],'2026-10-05T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-06-am-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','5 bikes, about $3,500, wildly different. Swipe for the five we pulled from 330 in the directory: ADO Air 20 Ultra folder (22kg, $3,499), AMPD Bros Chubbie 3 fat tyre (960Wh, $3,490), Aventon Aventure M (100Nm mid-drive, $3,499), Cube Supreme Hybrid ONE 500 (Bosch, $3,499) and Pedal Eagle ST ($3,399). Same money, 22kg to 44.5kg and 346Wh to 960Wh. All brand declared road-legal, no throttle. FINDER DATA, 330 bikes compared. Which one would you buy? Link in bio to compare them. @bikesonline.aus @aventon #ebike #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder #commuterebike',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-4.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-am-carousel-slide-5.jpg'],'2026-10-05T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-06-am-ig','roxy','[{"slide": 2, "username": "bikesonline.aus", "x": 0.4, "y": 0.52}, {"slide": 2, "username": "aventon", "x": 0.6, "y": 0.52}]'::jsonb),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','What kills an e-bike battery? Heat is the main enemy. Our battery care guide says a replacement battery is one of the most expensive parts on the bike, and a few habits are the difference between 3 years and 8: keep it out of hot cars and direct sun, avoid long stretches at 100%, avoid regular runs to 0%, and use the charger that came with the bike. If the case swells, it runs unusually hot on charge, or it has taken a knock, stop using it and contact the retailer or manufacturer. Full guide: https://ebikefinder.au/guides/guide-ebike-battery-care Which of these have you been guilty of? #ebike #ebikesafety',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-pm-image.jpg'],'2026-10-06T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-06-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','What kills an e-bike battery? Heat is the main enemy. A replacement battery is one of the priciest parts on the bike, and four habits decide whether it lasts 3 years or 8: keep it out of hot cars and full sun, avoid long stretches at 100%, avoid regular runs to 0%, and use the charger that came with the bike. Swollen, hot on charge or dropped? Stop using it and call the retailer. Bike shown: Trek Allant+ 7 Lowstep Gen 2. Which of these have you been guilty of? Send this to someone who leaves their battery in the car. Link in bio for the full guide. #ebike #ebikebattery #ebikesafety #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-06-tue-pm-image.jpg'],'2026-10-06T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-06-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','reel','Your phone, locked on. The GUB P19 Shock Absorbing Phone Holder is A$34.99 and sold and shipped by eBikeFinder from Australia. Spring loaded clamp for phones from 4.5 to 7.2 inches, a shock module plus four damping pads, one button release, a ball joint for one handed angle changes, a tool free strap for most bars and a top mount for an action camera or light. It is plastic (ABS and nylon) and about 219g, so the aluminium GUB P55 is the tougher step up. Shipping is $9.95, free over $60. Details checked 4 Oct 2026. https://ebikefinder.au/products/gub-p19-shock-absorbing-phone-holder What do you run your navigation on? #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-am-reel.mp4'],'2026-10-06T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-07-am-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','reel','Your phone, locked on. The GUB P19 Shock Absorbing Phone Holder, A$34.99, sold and shipped by eBikeFinder. Spring loaded clamp for phones from 4.5 to 7.2 inches (Pro Max and Ultra sizes included), a shock module plus four damping pads for rough roads, one button release, a ball joint to set your angle, a tool free strap for most bars and a top mount for an action camera or light. Real footage, shot on a real bike. Shipping is $9.95, free over $60. What do you run your navigation on? Send this to the mate whose phone bounces off the bars. Link in bio. #ebike #ebikeaccessories #phonemount #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-am-reel.mp4'],'2026-10-06T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-07-am-ig','roxy',null),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','750W throttle bike. Bike path. Queensland. Legal or not? Not legal. Queensland''s own rules say a device that can be ridden by throttle alone above 6km/h is illegal, and a motor capable of more than 250W is illegal whether or not it is locked to a lower limit. Police can seize and destroy clearly illegal devices and issue a $621 fine. Our law guide says the throttle rule is the same in every state, and NSW, Victoria and Queensland all treat a locked high power bike as illegal. The legal recipe: 250W continuous, assist that cuts out at 25km/h, throttle limited to 6km/h, plus an EN 15194 label in Queensland. The bike in the question is the ENGWE M20 2.0 (750W rear hub, $1,749 at PC Market, checked 27 Sep 2026), which eBikeFinder lists as off-road and private property only. Rules are changing fast, so confirm with your state transport authority. Check any bike: https://ebikefinder.au/is-my-ebike-legal-australia Would you have known? #ebike #ebikelaws',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-4.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-5.jpg'],'2026-10-07T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-07-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','750W throttle bike. Bike path. Queensland. Legal or not? Not legal. A bike you can ride on throttle alone above 6km/h is illegal in every state, and Queensland police can seize and destroy it with a $621 fine. Locking it to a lower speed does not fix it if the hardware can go faster. The legal recipe is 250W continuous, assist that stops at 25km/h, and a throttle that only pushes to 6km/h. Bike in the question: the ENGWE M20 2.0, $1,749, listed on eBikeFinder as private property only. Swipe for the rules. Would you have known? Send this to a mate eyeing a moped style bike. Link in bio for Is my e-bike legal. #ebike #ebikelaws #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-4.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-07-wed-pm-carousel-slide-5.jpg'],'2026-10-07T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-07-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','Fat tyres, 733Wh, $2,899 ride away through BikesOnline. Who is the Aventon Aventure 3 actually for? Value hunters who want a big battery and hydraulic discs on a fat tyre step-through: 250W, 69Nm, up to 105km claimed (best case), 34kg, throttle removed for the Australian market. The catch: it is available in every state and territory except NSW, where BikesOnline is awaiting NSW Fair Trading registration. Compliance is declared by the brand, so ask BikesOnline for the EN 15194 paperwork. Price and stock from bikesonline.com.au via our listing, checked 4 Oct 2026. Specs and the Aventure M comparison: https://ebikefinder.au/ebikes/aventon/aventure-3 Would you ride it? #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-08-thu-am-image.jpg'],'2026-10-07T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-08-am-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','Fat tyres, 733Wh, $2,899 ride-away. Who is the Aventon Aventure 3 actually for? Value hunters who want a big battery and hydraulic discs on a fat tyre step-through: 250W, 69Nm, up to 105km claimed, 34kg, throttle removed for Australia. The catch: it is not available in NSW yet, because BikesOnline is awaiting NSW Fair Trading registration. Would you ride it? Tag the mate who needs a fat tyre. Link in bio for the full specs and the Aventure M comparison. @bikesonline.aus @aventon #ebike #fattyre #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-08-thu-am-image.jpg'],'2026-10-07T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-08-am-ig','roxy','[{"username": "bikesonline.aus", "x": 0.4, "y": 0.55}, {"username": "aventon", "x": 0.62, "y": 0.55}]'::jsonb),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','reel','100km range? Not on your ride. Manufacturer range claims are almost always measured on the lowest assist level, on flat ground, with a light rider. Riding on the highest assist setting can roughly halve the range, a headwind has the same effect as a mild constant climb, and hills, stop start riding, cold and extra weight all cost more. Our range guide suggests planning on 50 to 70 percent of the advertised maximum. Work out your own band with the range calculator: https://ebikefinder.au/ebike-range-calculator What range does your bike really get? #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-08-thu-pm-reel.mp4'],'2026-10-08T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-08-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','reel','100km range? Not on your ride. Claimed range is measured on the lowest assist, on flat ground, with a light rider. Max assist can roughly halve it, a headwind acts like a constant climb, and hills, stop start riding and extra weight all draw more battery. Plan on 50 to 70% of the claimed number. Want yours? The eBikeFinder range calculator estimates a real band from battery size, rider weight, terrain and riding style. What range does your bike really get? Send this to someone shopping on the big number. Link in bio. #ebike #ebikerange #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-08-thu-pm-reel.mp4'],'2026-10-08T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-08-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','Can an e-bike replace your second car? Here is the 12 month maths, with the assumptions on show. eBikeFinder''s car vs e-bike calculator defaults: 16 km round trip, 5 days a week, 8 L/100km, $2.00 a litre, $8 a day parking, $3,000 e-bike, 10 Wh per km, $0.30 per kWh. Result: the car costs $2,746 a year to run ($666 fuel, $2,080 parking), the e-bike about $12 to charge, a saving of about $2,733 a year and a payback of about 13 months. Cargo bikes cost more, so payback stretches: the $5,999.99 Trek Fetch+ 2 (clearance price) is about 26 months on the same saving. This is running costs only, with no rego, insurance, servicing or depreciation. Bikes shown, with directory prices: Tern HSD P5i $7,495, Pedal Packer $4,300, Leitner Atlas $2,599, Trek Fetch+ 2 $5,999.99. Run your own numbers: https://ebikefinder.au/ebike-vs-car-cost-calculator Would you drop the second car? #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-am-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-am-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-am-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-am-carousel-slide-4.jpg'],'2026-10-08T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-09-am-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','Can an e-bike replace your second car? Here is the 12 month maths. On the eBikeFinder calculator defaults (16 km round trip, 5 days a week, 8 L/100km, $2.00 a litre, $8 a day parking) the car costs $2,746 a year to run: $666 fuel plus $2,080 parking. Charging an e-bike costs about $12 a year. That is a saving of about $2,733 a year, so a $3,000 bike pays back in about 13 months, and a $5,999.99 Trek Fetch+ 2 in about 26. Running costs only: rego, insurance, servicing and depreciation are not counted. Swipe for the bikes: Tern HSD P5i, Pedal Packer, Leitner Atlas, Trek Fetch+ 2. Would you drop the second car? Send this to the household''s other driver. Link in bio to run your own trip. #ebike #cargoebike #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder #familyebike',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-am-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-am-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-am-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-am-carousel-slide-4.jpg'],'2026-10-08T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-09-am-ig','roxy',null),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','Got a new e-bike, accessory or price change? Send it to us. eBikeFinder is Australia''s independent e-bike directory, and we are looking for launch bikes, demo bikes, new models, accessories, price changes and dealer openings. One bike can earn a directory profile, a written review, a video review, social content and a place in our comparisons. Brands and retailers, message this page. Riders, tell us which new bike you want us to look at next. Browse the directory: https://ebikefinder.au #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-pm-image.jpg'],'2026-10-09T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-09-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','Got a new e-bike? Send it to us. eBikeFinder is Australia''s independent e-bike directory, and we want launch bikes, demo bikes, new models, accessories, price changes and dealer openings. One bike can earn a directory profile, a written review, a video review, social content and a place in our comparisons. Brand or retailer? Message this page. Riders: tag the shop or brand you think we should look at. Which new bike do you want us to test next? Link in bio. #ebike #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder #ebikereview',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-09-fri-pm-image.jpg'],'2026-10-09T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-09-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','NEW IN THE ACT: electric cargo bikes became an eligible product under the ACT''s Sustainable Household Scheme on 21 September. Loans run from $2,000 to $20,000 at 3% interest, repayable over up to 10 years, with no establishment or account keeping fees. You do not need a driver licence to apply for an e-cargo bike. Applicants must meet Brighte''s standard credit criteria and the scheme guidelines, including a free one hour workshop. Households that applied or were approved before 1 July 2026 are capped at $15,000 across the scheme. Check the scheme''s eligibility rules and approved supplier requirements before you shop. Full story: https://ebikefinder.au/news/act-sustainable-household-scheme-ecargo-bike-loans-2026 Would you swap a car trip for a cargo bike? #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-am-image.jpg'],'2026-10-09T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-10-am-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','NEW IN THE ACT: e-cargo bikes now qualify for a 3% loan. Since 21 September, electric cargo bikes are an eligible product under the ACT''s Sustainable Household Scheme. Loans run from $2,000 to $20,000 at 3% interest over up to 10 years, with no establishment or account keeping fees, and you do not need a driver licence to apply. Applicants need to meet Brighte''s credit criteria and attend a free one hour workshop. The pitch is the second car: school drops and the grocery run. Canberra, would you swap a car trip for a cargo bike? Tag a Canberra family who should see this. Details in the News section, link in bio. #ebike #cargoebike #canberra #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-am-image.jpg'],'2026-10-09T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-10-am-ig','roxy',null),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','The lightest folding e-bike in the eBikeFinder directory weighs 15kg. We filtered the 330 bikes for folders that are in stock, brand declared Australian compliant and have a dated price, then sorted by weight. Under 21kg there are three: Leitner Aria (15kg, $1,299 ride-away, 245Wh, 50km claimed), Brompton C Line Electric (15.4kg, $7,300, 300Wh, 70km claimed) and ADO Air 20 Pro (20kg, $2,995, 346Wh, 100km claimed). A heavier, cheaper option is the Leitner Libelle (23.5kg, $1,650, 360Wh). Weights are manufacturer figures, ranges are claimed best case, and prices were checked on 27 Sep 2026. Which would you carry up the stairs? Browse the folders: https://ebikefinder.au/ebikes #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-pm-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-pm-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-pm-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-pm-carousel-slide-4.jpg'],'2026-10-10T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-10-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','The lightest folding e-bike in the directory weighs 15kg. Swipe for the three lightest we found among 330 bikes: Leitner Aria (15kg, $1,299, 245Wh), Brompton C Line Electric (15.4kg, $7,300, 300Wh) and ADO Air 20 Pro (20kg, $2,995, 346Wh, 100km claimed). Then a heavier, cheaper option: Leitner Libelle (23.5kg, $1,650). Method: folding, in stock, brand declared Australian compliant, price dated, sorted by weight. FINDER DATA, 330 bikes compared. Would you trade range for 15kg? Send this to someone with a flight of stairs. Link in bio. #ebike #foldingebike #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-pm-carousel-slide-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-pm-carousel-slide-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-pm-carousel-slide-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-10-sat-pm-carousel-slide-4.jpg'],'2026-10-10T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-10-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','Worth the extra $500? Reid Let''s Roll vs Reid Let''s Moto, both from Reid Cycles Australia. Let''s Roll Step-Through: $1,299.99 ride-away, 418Wh, 60km claimed, 40Nm hub drive, 28kg, 27.5 inch wheels. Let''s Moto Fat: $1,799.99 ride-away, 529Wh, 80km claimed, 42Nm hub drive, 28kg, 20 x 4.0 fat tyres. The extra $500 buys 111Wh, a claimed 20km and fat tyres, at the same weight. Prices checked on reidcycles.com.au on 4 Oct 2026 and specs from the eBikeFinder listings. Ranges are claimed best case. Reid is not currently shipping these to NSW pending NSW Fair Trading registration (listing checked 22 Sep 2026), so confirm with Reid before ordering. Compare them side by side: https://ebikefinder.au/compare?bikes=reid/lets-roll,reid/lets-moto Which would you pick? Reid Cycles. #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-11-sun-am-image.jpg'],'2026-10-10T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-11-am-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','Worth the extra $500? Reid Let''s Roll vs Reid Let''s Moto. The Let''s Roll step-through is $1,299.99 ride-away: 418Wh, 60km claimed, 40Nm, 28kg. The Let''s Moto fat tyre is $1,799.99: 529Wh, 80km claimed, 42Nm, 28kg. Same weight, same hub drive, so the extra $500 buys 111Wh, a claimed 20km and fat tyres. Both are not currently shipping to NSW per the listing, so check your state. Which would you pick? Send this to someone choosing between the two. @reidcycles Link in bio. #ebike #reidcycles #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-11-sun-am-image.jpg'],'2026-10-10T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-11-am-ig','roxy','[{"username": "reidcycles", "x": 0.3, "y": 0.42}]'::jsonb),
('982e3b99-127f-460b-95c6-d82a689efadc','image','The lightest 90Nm+ bike under $4,000 in the eBikeFinder directory is the VelectriX Ascent X: 95Nm Bafang M510 mid drive, 23.5kg, 504Wh battery, 70km claimed, $3,199 ride-away (listing checked 27 Sep 2026). Method: from 330 bikes we kept those under $4,000 with 90Nm or more that are in stock, brand declared Australian compliant and have a dated price, then sorted by weight. Next lightest is the Earth T-Rex at 26kg, then the Aventon Aventure M (33.1kg), Smartmotion Renegade (36kg) and AMPD Ace Pro (40kg). Weights and torque are manufacturer figures, range is claimed best case. Compare them: https://ebikefinder.au/compare?bikes=velectrix/ascent-x,earth/t-rex-trekking,aventon/aventure-m,smartmotion/renegade Do you want the torque or the lighter bike? #ebike #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-11-sun-pm-image.jpg'],'2026-10-11T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-11-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('d11766da-8e25-43c6-9cea-1c2e81264272','image','The lightest 90Nm+ bike under $4,000 in the directory is the VelectriX Ascent X: 95Nm Bafang M510 mid drive, 23.5kg, 504Wh, 70km claimed, $3,199 ride-away. Next lightest that passes the filter is the Earth T-Rex at 26kg, then the Aventon Aventure M (33.1kg), Smartmotion Renegade (36kg) and AMPD Ace Pro (40kg). Method: under $4,000, 90Nm or more, in stock, brand declared Australian compliant, price dated, sorted by weight. FINDER DATA, 330 bikes compared. Do you want the torque or the lighter bike? Send this to your trail riding mate. Link in bio. #ebike #emtb #ebikeaustralia #ebikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/ebikefinder/2026-10-11-sun-pm-image.jpg'],'2026-10-11T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-ebikefinder-2026-10-11-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image','57mm tyres. Gen 3 Grail. Canyon launched the third generation Grail on 17 September and the Australian site now lists four models from $3,499 to $9,000 AUD.

What changed: 57mm (2.25 inch) tyre clearance with 4mm of ISO clearance to spare, a stack 15mm lower than the previous Grail, a longer wheelbase, and one-by groupsets only so the drivetrain does not eat into tyre room. Complete bikes start from 8.39kg.
Why it matters: tyre volume is the biggest comfort and grip lever on rough gravel, and Canyon is no longer asking riders to choose between speed and width.
Who should care: gravel racers, and anyone watching the UCI Gravel World Championships in Nannup this weekend. Canyon says Rosa Klöser raced the new Grail CFR to victory at The Traka 360 on its debut.
Is it better? Canyon''s wind tunnel claim (faster than the competition at 35km/h) is its own data. Independent numbers will tell the real story.

Australian pricing from canyon.com/en-au, checked 4 October 2026: Grail CF 7 $3,499 (coming soon), CF SLX 7 Di2 $5,999 (coming soon), CF SLX 8 AXS $7,499, CFR Di2 $9,000. Canyon sells direct, so check sizes in stock before you plan around one.

Compare tyre clearance, gearing and price across the gravel bikes sold in Australia: bikefinder.au/gravel

What is the widest tyre you would run on gravel? #gravelbike #bikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/bikefinder/bf-01-grail-gen3.jpg'],'2026-10-04T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-bikefinder-2026-10-05-am-fb','roxy',null),
('32a573bb-697e-4c12-b64a-290a5991bbfc','image','57mm tyres. Gen 3 Grail. Canyon''s third generation gravel race bike clears 2.25 inch tyres, runs one-by only and starts at $3,499 AUD.

What changed: 57mm clearance, a stack 15mm lower than the old Grail, and complete bikes from 8.39kg.
Who should care: gravel racers. The UCI Gravel World Championships roll out in Nannup, WA this Saturday and Sunday, and the last Grail already has Worlds form.
Is it better? Canyon says it beat rivals in its own wind tunnel at 35km/h. We will believe it when someone else tests it.

Four models, $3,499 to $9,000 AUD, as listed on canyon.com/en-au on 4 Oct 2026. The CF 7 and CF SLX 7 Di2 are still marked coming soon.

