('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image','Most gravel bikes stop at 45mm. We ran the numbers on BikeFinder''s Gravel Finder: of the 26 gravel bikes with a listed maximum tyre clearance, 16 top out at 45mm, one at 47mm, five at 50mm and four at 53mm. Only 9 of 26 clear 50mm or more.

The widest: Giant Revolt and Liv Devote, at 53mm. Worth knowing before you buy: Giant says the Revolt''s 53mm applies with the flip chip in the long position, which Giant pairs with a longer wheelbase and added stability.

Why it matters this week: UCI Gravel World Championship riders hit Nannup on Saturday, and the new Canyon Grail now claims 57mm. Clearance is the number the market is racing on.

Method: BikeFinder Gravel Finder (bikefinder.au/gravel), max tyre clearance field, 26 of 34 gravel bikes with a listed value, checked 4 October 2026. Figures are researched from manufacturer and retailer sources and can vary by model year.

