('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image','Same $21,500. Heavier bike. Specialized released the gold Remco Evenepoel S-Works Tarmac SL9 LTD on 22 September. Only 100 numbered bikes are being made. In Australia it is $21,500.

The numbers, all from specialized.com/au (size 56 claimed weights, checked 4 October 2026):
Remco LTD: $21,500 AUD, 6.78kg, custom SRAM RED AXS Team Edition, Roval Rapide Sprint CLX wheels, 30mm Cotton tyres.
S-Works Tarmac SL9 RED AXS: $21,500 AUD, 6.6kg, Roval Rapide CLX III wheels.
Tarmac SL9 Expert SRAM Force AXS: $10,200 AUD, 7.55kg, Roval C38 wheels, FACT 10r frame.

What it means: the LTD is not lighter or faster than the standard S-Works. The wheels differ, so the 180g gap is not like for like, and at this price the paint and the number are a big part of what you are buying. The standard S-Works uses the same 687g FACT 12r frame.

If you want most of the bike for half the money, the Expert is the one to look at. If you want the gold one, check stock with a Specialized dealer soon.

See every Tarmac we track at bikefinder.au

Which would you buy, the gold one or the half price one? #specialized #bikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/bikefinder/bf-04-remco-sl9.jpg'],'2026-10-06T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-bikefinder-2026-10-06-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('32a573bb-697e-4c12-b64a-290a5991bbfc','image','Same $21,500. Heavier bike. Specialized''s gold Remco Evenepoel S-Works Tarmac SL9 LTD costs $21,500 AUD and weighs 6.78kg (size 56). The standard S-Works Tarmac SL9 with SRAM RED AXS also costs $21,500 and weighs 6.6kg.

What you are paying for: a numbered edition (only 100 made) and the gold to white paint. The Remco bike also runs deeper Roval Rapide Sprint CLX wheels, so the 180g gap is not like for like.

The other end of the range: the Tarmac SL9 Expert with SRAM Force AXS is $10,200 AUD and 7.55kg. Half the money, 950g more than the S-Works.

All weights are Specialized''s claimed figures at size 56, checked on specialized.com/au on 4 Oct 2026.

