('7a1b5eff-3026-4988-b5fd-5e42c8489b1c','image','Two aero bikes. Almost one price. Giant''s fourth generation Propel and Merida''s fifth generation Reacto have both landed in Australia, and the entry points are within a few hundred dollars of each other.

Giant Propel Advanced 1: $5,999 AUD RRP (Giant Australia). Shimano 105 Di2 12 speed, 36/52 chainrings, 11x36 cassette, Giant SLR 2 50mm carbon wheels, 28mm Gavia Course 0 tyres, up to 32mm.
Merida Reacto 6000: $5,899 to $6,299 AUD depending on the retailer (Bike Force Joondalup $5,899, 99 Bikes $6,199, Cycleworld $6,149 against a $6,299 list). Shimano 105 Di2 12 speed, 52/36 chainrings, Vision SC 60 carbon wheels, 28mm tyres, up to 32mm.

What it means: they match on groupset, tyre room and price. The gap is the wheels (50mm versus 60mm) and the gearing (lowest gear 1.00 on the Propel, 1.06 on the Reacto). Our read: Propel for hillier rides, Reacto for flat and fast.

All prices checked 4 October 2026. Gearing is derived from the published chainrings and cassette, not a ride test.

Compare more road bikes at bikefinder.au

Propel or Reacto? #roadbike #bikefinder',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/bikefinder/bf-08-propel-vs-reacto.jpg'],'2026-10-08T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-bikefinder-2026-10-08-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('32a573bb-697e-4c12-b64a-290a5991bbfc','image','Two aero bikes. Almost one price. The all-new Giant Propel Advanced 1 is $5,999 AUD RRP. The all-new Merida Reacto 6000 is listed from $5,899 to $6,299 AUD depending on the shop.

What they share: Shimano 105 Di2 12 speed, carbon frames, hydraulic discs, 28mm stock tyres and room for up to 32mm. A few years ago an aero bike meant skinny tyres. Not any more.
What differs: the Propel runs 50mm carbon wheels and a 1.00 lowest gear (36 by 36). The Reacto runs 60mm carbon wheels and a 1.06 lowest gear.

Our read: the Propel suits hillier days thanks to the lower gear and shallower wheels. The Reacto suits flat, fast riding with its deeper rims. The price is a tie.

Giant Australia RRP, and Merida prices from Bike Force Joondalup ($5,899), 99 Bikes ($6,199) and Cycleworld ($6,149, list $6,299), checked 4 Oct 2026. Gearing: BikeFinder data from chainring and cassette.

