('ace75e80-c5ea-41f9-a568-867d9baddf1a','reel','30 minutes. How far can you go?

By bike, about 7.5 to 9 km. By e-bike, about 10 to 12.5 km. By scooter, about 7.5 to 10 km.

The maths: flat route, no stops. Bike 15 to 18 km/h. E-bike 20 to 25 km/h, because the assist stops at 25 km/h. Scooter 15 to 20 km/h, and always under your state limit. Hills, crossings and crowds will change it.

So an 8 km trip to work is about 27 to 32 minutes by bike, 19 to 24 by e-bike and 24 to 32 by scooter. That is closer than you think.

Which one suits your trip? Find a ride at ridefinder.au, a bike at bikefinder.au, an e-bike at ebikefinder.au or a scooter at scootfinder.au.

Scenes are AI generated for illustration.

