('ace75e80-c5ea-41f9-a568-867d9baddf1a','image','Angaston to Nuriootpa. Barossa Valley, SA.

About 12 km return, 1.5 to 2 hours allowed, on a sealed shared rail trail with rolling grades. SA Tourism lists the Angaston to Nuriootpa section as 6 km, so allow about 12 km return, plus extra for any town detour.

Start at the old Angaston station precinct, the Barossa Adventure Station, with parking, toilets and picnic facilities. Expect road crossings, and keep something in reserve for the climb back. No winery stops are built into this outing, so plan those separately.

Who would you bring to the Barossa for this one?

