('ace75e80-c5ea-41f9-a568-867d9baddf1a','image','Same journey. Three ways. A 4 km Saturday coffee run.

Which suits this journey? Not which is best.

Bike: 13 to 16 minutes. You supply all the power, there is no charging, and a basket carries the run.
E-bike: 10 to 12 minutes. The motor takes the sting out of hills and headwinds. Charge it at home, and expect to pay more upfront.
Scooter: 12 to 16 minutes. Light and compact, with room for a backpack only. Check your state rules for where you can ride one.

The maths: flat 4 km, no stops. Bike 15 to 18 km/h, e-bike 20 to 25 km/h (the assist stops at 25 km/h), scooter 15 to 20 km/h and under your state limit.

Which one are you taking on Saturday? Compare at https://bikefinder.au, https://ebikefinder.au and https://scootfinder.au, then find the ride at https://ridefinder.au/rides/

Images are AI generated for illustration.

