('5919f089-e69f-47cb-ba1b-2ee465ccb995','image','A short coastal roll in Darwin. Nightcliff foreshore, NT.

Up to 4 km return, up to an hour, on a sealed shared path with gentle coastal grades. Start by Nightcliff Jetty, ride up to 2 km along the foreshore towards the pool and Rapid Creek, then roll back for a jetty view or a picnic. The jetty itself is not part of the cycling route.

Sunset draws a crowd, so allow time to finish riding before dark. Keep the coastal rest on land: follow the crocodile and marine hazard warnings, and do not turn it into an unplanned swim. Check City of Darwin notices before you go.

