('ace75e80-c5ea-41f9-a568-867d9baddf1a','image','The perfect Sunday morning loop. Kent Street Weir, Wilson, Perth WA.

About 4 km, 1.5 to 2 hours allowed, on the Butterflies, Birds and Bridges Trail: a mostly flat, hardened dual use loop through riverside woodland beside the Canning River. Finish at the weir for a picnic. DBCA lists toilets, sheltered picnic tables, barbecues and a playground at the weir.

Take the bridges slowly, dismount where space is tight or signs ask you to, and stay on the formed trail. Bridge surfaces can be slippery when damp. Check DBCA visitor notices after rain.

Who is your Sunday morning riding partner?

Full guide with maps and stops: https://ridefinder.au/rides/wa/kent-street-weir-loop/

Photo: Calistemon, CC BY-SA 4.0, via Wikimedia Commons.

