('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Public holiday Monday in NSW, SA, the ACT and QLD, so the backyard is open all day. Whip of the week: the licensed Arctic Cat Wildcat XL 24V. It is a two seater side by side with four motors (4WD), a 24V 7Ah battery, a 2.4GHz parent remote, seatbelts and large soft EVA tyres. Manufacturer age guidance is 3+ yrs and the combined max load is 60kg. Top speed is claimed at 8 km/h. It weighs 36kg, so plan where it lives. $649 at MC Wholesalers, $680 at Endless Toys, prices checked 27 Sept 2026. Full specs and both retailers: tinywhips.com.au/whips/arctic-cat-wildcat-xl-24v-two-seater-4wd-utv. Two riders, one whip: who gets the passenger seat? #tinywhips #kidsrideon',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-01-mon-am-whip-of-week.jpg'],'2026-10-04T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-05-am-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Four first whips, one 20kg limit. Every 6V starter we compared tops out at a 20kg max load, so check your child''s weight before you check the colour. Swipe for the four: Costway Toddler ATV 6V ($95.95, from 1.5 yrs), Peg Perego John Deere Mini Tractor 6V ($359 to $399.95, from 1.5 yrs), Rigo BMW S1000RR 6V Motorbike ($85 to $86.95, 3 to 4 yrs) and the Ausway Vespa PX150 6V ($94.97, 3 to 6 yrs). None of the four listings confirms a parent remote, so supervise within arm''s reach. Prices checked 26 to 27 Sept 2026 and they move, so confirm with the retailer. Filter by age at tinywhips.com.au/by-age. Which one would you start with? #tinywhips',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-02-mon-pm-s1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-02-mon-pm-s2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-02-mon-pm-s3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-02-mon-pm-s4.jpg'],'2026-10-05T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-05-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Remote control? Ask these 4 things before you buy a ride-on. 1) Is the remote included, or sold separately? 2) Is there an emergency stop button? 3) Can you lock the speed to low? 4) Can you buy a replacement remote, and does it need re-pairing? Of the 49 Australian listings we track, 29 confirm a parent remote, 18 say nothing and 2 have none, so never assume. Pictured: the Costway Caterpillar UTV 24V, which lists a parent remote, four 100W motors and a 50kg max load for ages 3 to 8, $393.95 at Costway Australia (price checked 26 Sept 2026, stock level unclear, so confirm with the retailer). Our parent remote guide: tinywhips.com.au/guides/parent-remote-controls-explained. What is the first thing you check on a listing? #tinywhips',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-03-tue-am-parent-remote.jpg'],'2026-10-05T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-06-am-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','reel','After dinner laps? Daylight saving started on Sunday in NSW, VIC, SA, the ACT and TAS, so there is more light after dinner. Four checks before the ride. 1) Stay inside the age and max load on the listing: Product Safety Australia says to check a toy suits the child''s age and to follow product guidelines for age and size. 2) Keep it off roads, driveways with moving cars, pools, ponds, steps and steep slopes. 3) Parent remote in hand, lowest speed for younger drivers. 4) Charge after every ride, with the supplied charger only. The full list is at tinywhips.com.au/safety. Scenery in this video is AI generated and no ride-ons are shown. What is your after dinner rule? #tinywhips',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-04-tue-pm-reel-evening-checks.mp4'],'2026-10-06T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-06-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Same Bluey ride-on, $100 apart. The Bluey 6V Ride-On Car (model 24320, 2 to 3 yrs, 25kg max load, 6V 4Ah battery) is $169 at Target Australia, $249.95 at BIG W Marketplace (sold by The Gamesmen, online only) and $269 at Toys"R"Us Australia (compare-at $299.99). All three checked 27 Sept 2026, so confirm price and stock before you buy. The listings do not confirm a parent remote. tinywhips.com.au does not currently earn commission from any of these retailers. Compare all three: tinywhips.com.au/whips/bluey-6v-ride-on-car-headstart. Cheapest wins, or does the retailer matter more to you? #tinywhips',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-05-wed-am-price-check.jpg'],'2026-10-06T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-07-am-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Two kids, one whip? Add the kilos first. A two seater''s max load is both riders combined, so two kids at 20kg each need a 40kg rating (our one seat vs two seat guide). Swipe for four two seaters: Twin Seater Deluxe 12V (40kg, $508 at Ride Ons, compare-at $589), Little Riders Can-Am UTV 24V (50kg, $699, made to order and ships within two weeks), Little Tacker Vulcan Carbon UTV 24V (60kg, ages 3 to 7, $629) and the Kahuna Mercedes-AMG G63 Two Seater 24V ($539 to $684), which publishes no max load or age, so ask the retailer before you buy. Prices checked 26 Sept 2026 and they move. See every two seater: tinywhips.com.au. How much do your two weigh combined? #tinywhips',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-06-wed-pm-s1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-06-wed-pm-s2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-06-wed-pm-s3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-06-wed-pm-s4.jpg'],'2026-10-07T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-07-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','11 weeks to Christmas, and three ride-ons are under $200. Swipe for the Rigo 12V Jeep ($183.95 at Kmart Marketplace, $191.95 at BIG W Marketplace, both online only; 3+ yrs, 30kg max load, parent remote), the Costway Mercedes-Benz SL500 12V ($189.95 at Costway Australia, listed as was $269.95; 3 to 8 yrs, 30kg, parent remote) and the Rigo 12V ATV Quad ($118.95 at Bunnings Marketplace, online only; 3+ yrs, 25kg, parent remote not stated). Prices checked 26 Sept 2026 and they move, so confirm price, stock and delivery before you buy. Every spec and retailer is at tinywhips.com.au. Which one is going under the tree? #tinywhips #christmas',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-07-thu-am-s1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-07-thu-am-s2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-07-thu-am-s3.jpg'],'2026-10-07T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-08-am-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Tractor Thursday: two ride-on tractors, $544 apart. The Ride Ons 12V Tractor and Trailer (photo shows Rovo badging) is $455 at RideOns.com.au (listed as was $619): 12V 7Ah, twin 25W motors, ages 3+, 30kg max load, parent remote, 3 to 6 km/h claimed. The Peg Perego John Deere Ground Force is $999 at Matty''s Toys and Baby (listed as was $1,149) and $999.96 at RDO Equipment: 12V, up to 7 yrs, 38kg max load, two forward speeds plus a parental lockout for second gear, and the listing does not confirm a parent remote. Prices checked 26 Sept 2026, so confirm stock and price. More farm and tradie rigs: tinywhips.com.au/ride-ons/farm-and-tradie-rigs. Which one would your little farmer pick? #tinywhips',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-08-thu-pm-tractor-thursday.jpg'],'2026-10-08T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-08-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Four checks before you buy a ride-on, new or second hand. 1) Check the age grading label suits your child. 2) Search the model on the ACCC recalls database (productsafety.gov.au/recalls). 3) Make sure the instructions are included. 4) Check every part works and nothing is broken. These come from the ACCC Product Safety kids'' toys guide (checked 4 Oct 2026). Our own safety notes for ride-ons, including remote, charger and helmet habits, are at tinywhips.com.au/safety. What is the first thing you check when you buy a ride-on? #tinywhips',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-09-fri-am-safety-checks.jpg'],'2026-10-08T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-09-am-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','reel','Weekend ready? Three habits before the first ride: parent remote in hand with the lowest speed for younger drivers, a helmet on (TinyWhips calls it a sensible habit on bikes, quads and karts), and keep ride-ons off the road and away from pools, ponds and steep slopes. Full checklist at tinywhips.com.au/safety. What is your first-ride-of-the-weekend routine? #tinywhips',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-10-fri-pm-reel-weekend-ready.mp4'],'2026-10-09T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-09-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Three ride-on motorbikes, from $94 to $190. Rigo Aprilia Dorsoduro 900 6V: $93.95 at BIG W Marketplace (Toys"R"Us $149.99), 3+ yrs, 20kg max load. Kahuna BMW HP4 12V three wheeler: $139 at Kahuna, $176 at Kids Car Sales, 3 to 8 yrs, max load not published. Kidbot 12V Motorcycle with training wheels: $189.95 at BIG W Marketplace, 3+ yrs, 30kg max load. None of the three confirms a parent remote in the listing. Prices checked 26 and 27 Sept 2026, so confirm before you buy. TinyWhips notes a helmet is a sensible habit on bikes, quads and karts (tinywhips.com.au/safety). Which bike would your little rider choose?',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-11-sat-am-s1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-11-sat-am-s2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-11-sat-am-s3.jpg'],'2026-10-09T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-10-am-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Weekend pick: the Peg Perego Corral T-Rex 12V quad, $1,080 at Kids Car Sales (in stock when checked). Ages 3+, 40kg max load, 12V 8Ah sealed lead acid battery, two 165W motors, low and high gears (3.4 and 6.7 km/h claimed), pedal accelerator that brakes when released. One retailer listed, and the listing does not confirm a parent remote. Price checked 26 Sept 2026, so confirm stock and price. Would you pay premium for the brand name? tinywhips.com.au',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-12-sat-pm-corral-t-rex.jpg'],'2026-10-10T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-10-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Sunday family cruiser: the Mercedes-AMG G63 Oversize 24V two seater, $858 at Ride Ons (listed was $1,189). Ages 3 to 7, 60kg max load, two seats, 24V system with four 50W motors advertised as 4WD, parent remote, 2 to 4 km/h, up to 1.5 hours claimed. Battery capacity (Ah) is not published, so treat runtime as a claim. Price checked 26 Sept 2026, so confirm stock and price. Two kids, one G63: who is riding shotgun? tinywhips.com.au',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-13-sun-am-g63-oversize.jpg'],'2026-10-10T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-11-am-fb','roxy',null),
('bfa8b5d2-ad84-4ecf-804c-e1f9b2f8f5c5','image','Sunday night: charge it before Monday. Four battery habits from the TinyWhips battery guide (updated 25 Sept 2026): recharge after every ride rather than leaving the battery flat, use only the supplied charger or an exact specification replacement, do not leave it on a basic charger for days unless the manual says the charger is designed for that, and store the car somewhere dry and away from direct heat. Always follow the manual for charging times. The quad shown is the Kahuna GTS99 12V, used as illustration only. What is your Sunday night ride-on routine? tinywhips.com.au',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@76559cb/posts/2026-10-05/tinywhips/post-14-sun-pm-charge-night.jpg'],'2026-10-11T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-tinywhips-2026-10-11-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image','Silver Cross Jet 5: $300 off. The Space colourway is $499 (was $799 RRP) on silvercross.com.au, and it is a pre-order with stock due mid November. Jet 5 weighs 7.2 kg, folds to 25 x 37 x 60 cm and runs from birth to 22 kg. Silver Cross calls it cabin size, but airlines decide what they accept, so check with yours. Full details at pramkin.com.au. Silver Cross prices checked 4 October 2026. A price change, not a recommendation. Who is travelling with a pram this summer? #pramkin #pricewatch',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-am-price-watch-jet5.jpg'],'2026-10-04T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-05-am-fb','roxy',null),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image','Silver Cross Jet 5: $300 off. The Space colourway is $499 (was $799 RRP) on silvercross.com.au, and it is a pre-order with stock due mid November. Jet 5 weighs 7.2 kg, folds to 25 x 37 x 60 cm and runs from birth to 22 kg. Check the colourway and the dates before you order. Fold size and weight details at the link in bio. Send this to someone planning a trip with a baby. #pramkin #pricewatch #travelstroller #ausparents',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-am-price-watch-jet5.jpg'],'2026-10-04T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-05-am-ig','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image','Which car seat, which stage? The NSW rules, from Transport for NSW: up to 6 months must use a rear-facing seat. From 6 months to 4 years, a rear-facing seat or a forward-facing seat with an inbuilt harness. From 4 to 7 years, a forward-facing seat with a harness or an approved booster. Children 7 and over who are too small for a seatbelt should use a booster or harness, and 145 cm is the suggested minimum height for an adult belt. To be approved, a seat must meet AS/NZS 1754. Examples shown are Maxi-Cosi Australia listings (Mico 12 LX Pro $459, Pria LX $599, Tuva $529, Rodi $179, all on special, prices checked 4 October 2026). Brand names are listings, not endorsements. Rules differ slightly by state, so check yours. Which stage are you shopping for? pramkin.com.au #pramkin #carseatsafety',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-pm-car-seat-stages-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-pm-car-seat-stages-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-pm-car-seat-stages-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-pm-car-seat-stages-4.jpg'],'2026-10-05T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-05-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image','Which car seat, which stage? The NSW rules in four steps. Up to 6 months: a rear-facing seat, like the Maxi-Cosi Mico 12 LX Pro capsule (birth to about 12 months, $459 on special, was $699). 6 months to 4 years: rear-facing, or forward-facing with an inbuilt harness, like the Maxi-Cosi Pria LX ($599, was $849). 4 to 7 years: a harnessed seat or an approved booster, like the Tuva ($529) or Rodi ($179). Then 145 cm is the suggested minimum for an adult seatbelt. Every seat must meet AS/NZS 1754. Rules differ slightly by state, so check yours. Link in bio for fit and boot notes. Send this to a parent-to-be. #pramkin #carseatsafety #babycarseat #ausparents',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-pm-car-seat-stages-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-pm-car-seat-stages-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-pm-car-seat-stages-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-05-pm-car-seat-stages-4.jpg'],'2026-10-05T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-05-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image','Pre-loved car seat? Five checks. From Kidsafe Victoria: a second-hand seat is fine only if it meets Australian Standard AS/NZS 1754 (sticker present and readable), has a clear history with no crash, includes all original parts and the instruction manual, is under 10 years old (check the manufacture date on the shell or label), and shows no cracks, stress marks or damaged straps. If the seller is unsure about the history, keep looking. Kidsafe Victoria''s Safe Seats, Safe Kids fitters can inspect a seat and check its age. Seat shown is a Cybex Cloud Q for illustration, not an endorsement. Anything you would add to the list? pramkin.com.au #pramkin #carseatsafety',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-06-am-preloved-seat-checks.jpg'],'2026-10-05T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-06-am-fb','roxy',null),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image','Pre-loved car seat? Five checks. Kidsafe Victoria says a second-hand seat can be a smart saving if it meets AS/NZS 1754 with a readable sticker, has a clear history with no crash, includes all original parts and the manual, is under 10 years old, and has no cracks, stress marks or frayed straps. Not sure? An accredited fitter can check the age and condition. Seat shown: Cybex Cloud Q, not an endorsement. Link in bio for more. Send this to a friend about to buy second-hand. #pramkin #carseatsafety #secondhandbaby #ausparents',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-06-am-preloved-seat-checks.jpg'],'2026-10-05T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-06-am-ig','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','reel','3 checks before you buy a pram. 1. Measure your boot, then compare it with the folded size. 2. Check the weight in kg, because you will lift it every day. 3. Ask what “from birth” includes: a bassinet, an insert or a flat recline. Pramkin lists the folded size, weight, newborn setup and price of 50+ prams, with the source and check date behind every number: pramkin.com.au. Which check would you add? #pramkin #pramshopping',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-06-pm-three-checks-reel.mp4'],'2026-10-06T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-06-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','reel','3 checks before you buy a pram. 1. Measure your boot, then compare it with the folded size. 2. Check the weight in kg, because you will lift it every day. 3. Ask what “from birth” includes: a bassinet, an insert or a flat recline. Every number on Pramkin has a source and a check date. Folded sizes, weights and newborn setups for 50+ prams at the link in bio. Which check would you add? #pramkin #pramshopping #newparents #ausmums',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-06-pm-three-checks-reel.mp4'],'2026-10-06T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-06-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image','What Australia’s pram standard checks. Product Safety Australia says a mandatory safety standard applies to prams and strollers, based on AS/NZS 2088. It sets requirements for harnesses (to stop falls), brakes and tether straps (to stop roll-aways), head barriers and foot enclosures (body entrapment) and small gaps (finger entrapment), and prams must be permanently marked with the maker, importer or supplier and the model. The standard is a minimum, not a ranking, so Pramkin never says one pram is safer than another. Always follow your pram’s manual. Pram shown for illustration only: Cybex Eezy S Twist+ 2, a listing not an endorsement. What should we explain next? pramkin.com.au #pramkin #pramsafety',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-am-pram-standard.jpg'],'2026-10-06T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-07-am-fb','roxy',null),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image','What Australia’s pram standard checks. A mandatory safety standard applies to prams and strollers sold here, based on AS/NZS 2088. It covers harnesses (to stop falls), brakes and tether straps (to stop roll-aways), head barriers and foot enclosures (body entrapment), small gaps (finger entrapment) and permanent marking with the maker or importer and the model. It does not rank one pram above another, so always read your pram’s manual too. Pram shown for illustration: Cybex Eezy S Twist+ 2, not an endorsement. Link in bio. Send this to a parent-to-be. #pramkin #pramsafety #babygear #ausparents',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-am-pram-standard.jpg'],'2026-10-06T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-07-am-ig','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image','Prams for rough walks: three to compare. UPPAbaby Ridge V2 (13.7 kg, $1,399 RRP, seat from 6 months, bassinet extra), Thule Urban Glide 3 (11.9 kg, $1,499.95 RRP) and Thule Spring 2 (10.8 kg, $1,099.95 RRP, bassinet $469.95 extra). Folded sizes are on each slide. All-terrain is not the same as jogging-approved: only run with a pram the maker approves for running, and follow its minimum age. Prices are RRP from the makers'' Australian sites, checked 4 October 2026. Brand names are listings, not endorsements. Where do you walk most, gravel, grass or sand? pramkin.com.au #pramkin #prams',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-pm-rough-walks-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-pm-rough-walks-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-pm-rough-walks-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-pm-rough-walks-4.jpg'],'2026-10-07T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-07-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image','Prams for rough walks: three to compare before the weekend. UPPAbaby Ridge V2, 13.7 kg, folds to 49.5 x 65 x 91.4 cm with the seat on, $1,399 RRP (seat from 6 months, bassinet extra). Thule Urban Glide 3, 11.9 kg, folds to 88 x 58 x 31 cm, $1,499.95 RRP. Thule Spring 2, 10.8 kg, folds to 75 x 45 x 39 cm, $1,099.95 RRP (bassinet $469.95 extra). All-terrain is not the same as jogging-approved: only run with a pram the maker approves for running, and follow its minimum age. Link in bio to compare. Send this to someone with a gravel path to conquer. #pramkin #allterrainpram #prams #ausparents',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-pm-rough-walks-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-pm-rough-walks-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-pm-rough-walks-3.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-07-pm-rough-walks-4.jpg'],'2026-10-07T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-07-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image','Your pram, in bags of sugar. Cybex Libelle: 6 kg, so 6 bags. iCandy Core 2: 7.8 kg, about 8 bags. iCandy Peach 7: 12.9 kg, about 13 bags. Weights come from the Pramkin listings, last checked 25 to 28 September 2026. Brand names are listings, not endorsements. How many bags can you lift into your boot? pramkin.com.au #pramkin #prams',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-08-am-sugar-bags.jpg'],'2026-10-07T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-08-am-fb','roxy',null),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image','Your pram, in bags of sugar. The Cybex Libelle is 6 kg, the iCandy Core 2 is 7.8 kg and the iCandy Peach 7 is 12.9 kg. That is 6, about 8 and about 13 bags of 1 kg sugar. Picture lifting that into the boot, then check the weight before you buy. Link in bio to compare weights. Send this to someone who is still choosing. #pramkin #prams #newparents #ausparents',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-08-am-sugar-bags.jpg'],'2026-10-07T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-08-am-ig','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image','Rear-facing myths, answered. Legs look squashed? Kidsafe VIC says bent, crossed or resting legs are normal and safe, and rear-facing protects the head, neck and spine. Want them to see out the window, or turning one or two? Age is not the cue. Let the shoulder height markers on the seat lead, which AS/NZS 1754 requires. If you cannot see them, raise the headrest. Not sure? Book a fitter check. Seats shown are Maxi-Cosi Raia 360 GCELL and Pria LX GCELL listings, not endorsements. Which myth have you heard? pramkin.com.au #pramkin #carseatsafety',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-08-pm-rear-facing-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-08-pm-rear-facing-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-08-pm-rear-facing-3.jpg'],'2026-10-08T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-08-pm-fb','roxy',null),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image','Rear-facing myths, answered. Their legs look squashed? Bent, crossed or resting on the seat back is normal, says Kidsafe VIC. A better view, or turning one or two? Neither is the cue. The real cue is the shoulder height markers on your seat label, which AS/NZS 1754 requires. Raise the headrest if it hides them. Not sure? Book a fitter check. Seats shown: Maxi-Cosi Raia 360 GCELL and Pria LX GCELL. Link in bio. Send this to a parent with a toddler. #pramkin #carseatsafety #rearfacing #ausparents',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-08-pm-rear-facing-1.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-08-pm-rear-facing-2.jpg','https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-08-pm-rear-facing-3.jpg'],'2026-10-08T07:32:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-08-pm-ig','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','image','Ocarro 2: pram or bundle? Mamas & Papas Australia lists the Ocarro 2 pram with seat at $1,495.95 and the carrycot at $499.95, which is $1,995.90 bought separately. The bundle with carrycot and cup holder is $1,995.95. Car seat adaptors are $59.95 extra. RRP, checked 4 October 2026, and prices change. Brand names are listings, not endorsements. Which would you pick, the pram alone or the bundle? pramkin.com.au #pramkin #pricewatch',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-09-am-ocarro-price-watch.jpg'],'2026-10-08T22:00:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-09-am-fb','roxy',null),
('162784a0-7283-4ea7-a878-6dba86e08d70','image','Ocarro 2: pram or bundle? The Mamas & Papas Ocarro 2 pram with seat is $1,495.95. The carrycot is $499.95 on its own, so both bought separately come to $1,995.90. The bundle with carrycot and cup holder is $1,995.95. Car seat adaptors are $59.95 extra. Prices are RRP, checked 4 October 2026. Link in bio to compare. Send this to someone choosing a newborn setup. #pramkin #pricewatch #prams #ausparents',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-09-am-ocarro-price-watch.jpg'],'2026-10-08T22:02:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-09-am-ig','roxy',null),
('8bbd00e2-9b5c-4893-b2cc-295c843e7926','reel','Rough walk pram? Check three things. 1. Weight: the Thule Spring 2 is 10.8 kg. 2. The fold: 75 x 45 x 39 cm. 3. Running: only run with a pram the maker approves for running, and follow its minimum age. Thule Spring 2 RRP $1,099.95, checked 4 October 2026 (bassinet $469.95 extra). Compare rough walk prams: pramkin.com.au. Brand names are listings, not endorsements. Where do you walk most, gravel, grass or sand? #pramkin #prams',array['https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/tbhglobal/cartell-social-media@6d84380/posts/2026-10-05/pramkin/2026-10-09-pm-rough-walks-reel.mp4'],'2026-10-09T07:30:00+00','queued','w1005-pramkin-2026-10-09-pm-fb','roxy',null),
