('e98d115c-09ce-4c5f-bf24-4c5d3df31147','image','WE SAID WHAT WE SAID.

1. Brunch is a business model, not a meal. Four hours, forty minutes of eating.
2. "Still or sparkling?" should come with a price. Asking twice should come with an apology.
3. "Your table is held for 15 minutes" is a threat, not a policy.
4. The last croquette is never shared. It is negotiated.

Which one did we get wrong? Best counter argument gets the pin.

