('e98d115c-09ce-4c5f-bf24-4c5d3df31147','image','VENUE SPOTLIGHT: Gymkhana, DIFC.

Indian cooking in a club inspired room, open at Gate Village since 1 September. Two ground floor dining rooms with lantern lighting and patterned ceilings, then a lower level with mirrored ceilings, chandeliers and a peacock bar. The menu runs from chaat style sharing plates and tandoori grills to classic curries and biryanis, plus dishes made for the Dubai room.

Good to know: the London original holds two Michelin stars, but those stay in London. Book this one for the room and the cooking, and check the current Dubai menu and prices with the venue before you go.

Where is your Friday night going? Send this to the person who picks the restaurant.

